{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1tprKAB99829FgjXcn6D9","type":"tool_result","content":"# Authorization and Security Considerations\n\nUnder the heading \"Authorization and security considerations,\" the document states:\n\n\"Access to `kubectl port-forward` is controlled by Kubernetes authorization mechanisms like Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).\"\n\nIt also specifies: \"To use `kubectl port-forward`, a user must have permission to access the target resource (for example, a Pod or Service) and the `portforward` subresource. Typical required permissions include `get` on `pods` and `create` on `pods/portforward`.\"\n\nAdditionally: \"Cluster administrators should carefully restrict these permissions, as port-forwarding can provide direct network access to workloads and may bypass network-level controls.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b156e7c-433e-416d-a6d5-5879b6834809","uuid":"c19fbd02-0ab7-409f-870c-d2cc33c0de6b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:52:21.404Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":5837,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Authorization and Security Considerations\n\nUnder the heading \"Authorization and security considerations,\" the document states:\n\n\"Access to `kubectl port-forward` is controlled by Kubernetes authorization mechanisms like Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).\"\n\nIt also specifies: \"To use `kubectl port-forward`, a user must have permission to access the target resource (for example, a Pod or Service) and the `portforward` subresource. Typical required permissions include `get` on `pods` and `create` on `pods/portforward`.\"\n\nAdditionally: \"Cluster administrators should carefully restrict these permissions, as port-forwarding can provide direct network access to workloads and may bypass network-level controls.\"","durationMs":2038,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/tasks/access-application-cluster/port-forward-access-application-cluster.